# What is NOT part of the public website.
#
# wrangler.jsonc sets the asset directory to "." (the repo root), so without
# this file every file in the repo is published to siteflyer.com. Two things
# went wrong because of that:
#
#   1. Cloudflare's cloud build runs `npx wrangler deploy`, which installs
#      wrangler into the repo directory. wrangler then tried to publish its own
#      node_modules and failed with "Asset too large" (25 MiB per-asset limit).
#      That is why deploying from a laptop worked and the cloud build did not.
#
#   2. Internal files were served publicly: copy drafts in attached_assets/,
#      agent notes in .agents/, STYLE-GUIDE.md, wrangler.jsonc and src/worker.js
#      all returned 200 on the live domain.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   partials/  - src/worker.js fetches partials/footer through the asset
#                binding to inject the shared footer. Ignoring it removes the
#                footer from all 56 pages.
#   components/ - the component gallery is a working reference the team opens.

# build and tooling
node_modules
.git
.wrangler
.cache
.upm
.config
.local

# agent and editor working files
.agents
.canvas
artifacts
attached_assets
screenshots

# source and config, not website content
src
wrangler.jsonc
package.json
package-lock.json
.replit
replit.nix
.deploy-check

# documentation
*.md
